  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is undergoing a transition after Gibran Rakabuming Raka officially resigned from his position as Vice President. In response to the vacancy, the People's Consultative Assembly has initiated a selection procedure, with plans to finalize a successor in early December 2026 based on two candidates proposed by President Prabowo. While some political entities have reaffirmed their commitment to the current administration, observers are monitoring the potential economic implications, particularly regarding market stability and investment confidence. Alongside the political proceedings, media coverage has focused on the standard protocols associated with such departures, including the specific retirement facilities and security arrangements provided to former officeholders under national regulations. Officials and various political figures have publicly called for a focus on public welfare and an orderly transition to ensure government continuity during this period.",
